# THE CALL MUST BE BARE, IN ITS OWN PROCESS. The first version of this seed ran
# `_deliver_launch_prompt … || _rc=$?` — an OR-list, which SUSPENDS errexit inside the
# function. So the seed written to enforce the errexit hazard was written in the one
# shape AGENTS.md says cannot show it ("Only a BARE call proves set -e safety — a
# failing command aborts ONLY in statement position; fn || … masks it"). Reviewer
# proved the gap by injecting a bare `false` into the function: the seed still passed.
#
# The real function is therefore run BARE in a fresh `bash -e`, and the PROCESS status
# is read from outside. The `|| _rc=$?` below is on the CHILD PROCESS, which is exactly
# where masking is harmless — the errexit under test lives inside it.
_dlp() { # <submit_rc> -> rc|file|event
