# ── the emission list is what keeps a LIVE helper working ────────────────────────
# A generated helper carries ONLY the functions its `declare -f` list names, and a
# name missing from that list breaks the helper AT RUNTIME while this suite stays
# green, because the suite calls the function straight out of ae.
#
# The specimen that stood here was `_send-deliver` — since A.1 the only agent-facing
# helper with a bash BODY left to break. B glue cut 1 removed it: the core delivers
# in-process, so that entry is not generated at all, and NO agent-facing helper has a
# bash body any more. The invariant did not move, it generalised, and the guards that
# carry it now are the four above ("Generalized emission-completeness guards"): every
# helper list ends with its main, every emitted name has exactly one definition, the
# template helper_* set equals the emitted set, and the TRANSITIVE closure holds for
# every artifact. Those cover `_lib` and the watchdog, which is where the bodies live.
assert_eq "send-deliver emission: the internal delivery entry is not generated at all" "0" \
